text: >-
  September 10, 2025

  9/10/25,3:17PM

  Charlie Kirk got shot

  9/10/25,3:44 PM

  Dead

  9/10/25,4:40PM

  I just saw the video holy shit

  Rip | guess

  Bro didn't deserve to go out like that sad

  zealous_monkey_55095 9/11/25,8:57 PM

  Hey guys, I have bad news for you all. it was me at

  UVU yesterday. im sorry for all of this. im

  surrendering through a sheriff friend in a few

  moments. thanks for all the good times and laugh

  you've all been so amazing

  newsweek.com

  everything

  The specific confession you're asking about-the one timestamped at 7:57 PM MDT

  (Utah time) on September 11, 2025—comes from that Discord group chat. In it,
  the

  account attributed to Robinson (username: zealous_monkey_55095) wrote to his
  friends:

  "Hey guys, I have bad news for you all. It was me at UVU yesterday. im sorry
  for all of

  this. im surrendering through a sheriff friend in a few moments. thanks for
  all the

  good times and laughs, you've all been so amazing, thank you all for
  everything."

  Why is this known and not just rumor?

  • Court documents and unsealed search warrants: Prosecutors have included

  these Discord messages in charging documents and warrants. Robinson's

  roommate showed investigators the chats on his screen and allowed photos to be

  taken as evidence. Court filings explicitly reference the 7:57 p.m. message
  and tie it

  to Robinson. deseret.com

  • Mainstream reporting: Outlets including the Washington Post, CNN, New York

  Times, BBC, ABC News, Deseret News, and others have reported the exact

  message, citing law enforcement sources, court records, and screenshots they

  reviewed. FBI Director Kash Patel even confirmed the Discord confession in

  congressional testimony. cnn.com

  • Independent journalist Ken Klippenstein's work: On September 16, 2025,

  Klippenstein published an exclusive Substack article titled "Exclusive: Leaked

  Messages from Charlie Kirk Assassin." He obtained the full Discord chat logs

  (including the confession) directly from a source connected to the group and
  also

  interviewed one of Robinson's childhood friends. The screenshots he released

  match the ones referenced in court docs and other reporting. His article is
  the

  primary public source of the actual chat images you're seeing here.

  newsweek.com
